# DEIFIED iOS/Android 2026

Cross-platform app project (targeting 2026 release) with integrated recurring support.

The advanced nature of this design of this software leads to optimal end-user experience. The canon is layered in a way that
the knowledge herein is accessible (EASY TO UNDERSTAND) for the first time user- or the expert in theology looking for nuances in 
understanding before unthought of in their own practices.

Why? Because the user drives the car. You ask the questions, God does the answering.

All user data is encrypted with highest known cryptology presently known to mankind. The cryptology can be broken by no man, nor government.

The Creator of this site invites ALL comeers to a challenge.  The creator of this site is a South Dakota-raised Enrollemd Member of the Turtle Mountain Band of Chippewa Tribe and 
9th Degree Midewiwin (Grand Medicine Society) Medicine Man. He talks to Jesus.

If you can break the cryptology that protects user data you gain 5% equity in the company after 
thorough review of your processes. Maybe wait til it catches fire though. More lucrative. I will be right here waiting for you. - Mide

## Mission / Reveal
When Faith holds, the truth will reveal itself. Join all of us on the divine journey; the journey in which we must, as God demands, bear maximal responsibility
for our lives. Christ beared the maximal responsibility for his life by bearning a cross for the rest of the world.

Christ did not and does not discriminate by culture, or color of skin; as the true Son of God, he represents what God expects of us all. Demanding
the most from his only begotten Son. 

We aren't Christ, but we can aim toward that ideal: take maximal responsibility for your own life
(flaws, mistakes, potential), your family, community, and the world as much as you can bear.

Truth Will Prevail. Honesty prevails.  

The problem with people in society today? They don't look low enough for Jesus—He is found in humility, among the lowly and broken.  
In pride we miss Him; in humility we find Him. God may be quiet, but He carries a big stick.

